    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-7820",
      "problem": "Plot the graph of $x= \\dfrac{1}{2}y - \\sqrt y\\,$ by completing the following table:\n\n| **$y$** | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ |  |  |  |  |",
      "worked_solution": "To graph this curve, we can start by calculating the value of $x$ for various values of $y,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=0 & \\,⟶\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0-\\sqrt{0}=0 \\\\ y=1 & \\,⟶\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1-\\sqrt{1}=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ y=4 & \\,⟶\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4-\\sqrt{4}=0 \\\\ y=16 & \\,⟶\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 16-\\sqrt{16}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can summarize these results in the following table:\n\n| **$y$** | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-\\dfrac12$ | $0$ | $4$ |\n\nSo, we have the following points:\n\n$$\n(0,0), \\quad \\left(-\\dfrac 12,1\\right), \\quad (0,4), \\quad (4,16).\n$$\n\nIf we plot these points and connect them with a smooth curve, we get the following graph:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14240562/assets/709bfcd1e69a0e4fd88d95fb9d8592de93921fad230b5f892059525871dc50fb.png)",
